The Apple Watch Series 12 and Ultra 4 offer a range of new health and fitness features. Here's everything that's new.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Apple-Watch-Series-12-2up-260909-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="2560" height="1440" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063392" /><br/>
Apple today revealed the following features for the two new devices:<br/>
<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li><strong>New "Health Sensing System"</strong>: A redesigned sensor architecture with three main improvements, including increased electrode surface area for better ECG skin contact, photodiodes arranged in a ring for more efficient light capture, and larger, more power-efficient green LEDs for accurate heart rate readings during motion.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Continuous heart rate sensing</strong>: Heart rate is now measured every five seconds throughout the day, 60 times more frequently than before, viewable via a new watch face complication.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Higher-frequency HRV</strong>: Heart rate variability is sampled up to 24 times more often, with separate recovery and overall HRV values shown in a new section of the Heart Rate app.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Daytime vitals view</strong>: A new toggle lets users switch between overnight and daytime vitals, potentially catching shifts in metrics before they show up in overnight readings.</li><br/>
<li><strong>VO2 Max test</strong>: A new test has users set up their iPhone to watch them perform a series of exercises, delivering results immediately alongside data from their Apple Watch.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Most accurate step tracking</strong>: A redesigned pedometer model with new machine learning algorithms improves distance accuracy for indoor workouts and all-day step counts.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Steps complication</strong>: A brand-new watch face complication, enabled by the S11 chip, lets users track their step count in real time.</li><br/>
<li><strong>Longer workout battery life</strong>: Up to 10 hours during an outdoor workout, 25% more than the previous model, with 15 minutes of charging now delivering up to 12 hours of extra battery. The Apple Watch Ultra 4 goes further, with up to 50 hours of everyday battery life, 84 hours in Low Power Mode, and a new Max Extended Workout mode rated for up to 45 hours of outdoor tracking; 15 minutes of charging adds up to 18 hours of battery.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
